[{:db/id 17592186179482 :question/problem "Consider the circle $S$ and vector field $\\mathbf F$ shown below. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $C$ is negative\n\nII. The flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nIII. The flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $-C$ is positive\n\n![](images/7e/7e7fbe6aaf1310b186344a3cf5a127075f11a86b51db2e687ddc7035d5d890f8.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179647 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f9f7d0a1-c461-5247-ab30-95b875686e93"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186420914 :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f1d25942ae680c068b587f38bfbc968c8850b8fa2db2003e994e1ec32dad892.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is positive\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is negative" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186420911 :question/problem "![](images/01/01d8d85064253b9241b1fd93c22381897f23556d6e02c5c2c0161c94cee3bbdf.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is negative\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186420912 :question/problem "![](images/af/afaec113101f1a63134d2b1cb5c9744b93f9b84dabafaa205780d2dc5b49a7bc.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is positive\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186420910 :question/problem "![](images/28/28a7eb32cfcd800c907e9f4af927eca7bd8616d36162682413db62a9feabefbb.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the clockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is negative\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180031 :question/problem "![](images/e6/e679efaa2612d45bbfe8b918de7148853b64eaf530af34a525ef1735e0946b09.png)\n\nConsider the circle $S$ and vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be any path where $S$ is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is positive\n\nII. The flux of $F$ across $C$ is zero\n\nIII. The flux of $F$ across $-C$ is positive" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-f9f7d0a1-c461-5247-ab30-95b875686e93" :question/id #uuid "f9f7d0a1-c461-5247-ab30-95b875686e93" :question/math-academy-id "q-226134" :question/problem "![](images/95/958965484cd271c5eb7ccfc8bf913386e57b9b733719885d232e562063969ca8.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F=-x\\,i+2y\\,j$ and a square $C$ with side length $4$ centered at $O,$ as shown above. Calculate the flux of $F$ across $C.$\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that, due to symmetry, the flux is equal across the vertical sides, and similarly for the horizontal sides.*" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$ In this case, we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{4}}F\\cdot {n}_{4}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere the sides ${C}_{i}$ and unit vectors ${n}_{i}$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/3b/3bd953b7fb02b90a55a29bea6f58ff9bd8bab77d62b1df1c547ca899656d37a3.png)\n\nWe compute this integral in two stages. \n\n- First, consider the side ${C}_{1}.$ We have that ${n}_{1}=i,$ and therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}(-x\\,i+2y\\,j)\\cdot i\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}x\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a line integral with respect to arc length, which we can evaluate in the usual way. Parameterizing the side ${C}_{1},$ we have\n\n$$\nr(t)=2\\,i+t\\,j,\\,⇒\\,{r}^{′}(t)=j,\\,t\\in [-2,2].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}x\\,\\text{d}s & =-{\\int }_{-2}^{2}2\\cdot ||{r}^{′}(t)||\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy symmetry, the flux integral across the side ${C}_{3}$ must be the same. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot {n}_{3}\\,\\text{d}s=-8.\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider the side ${C}_{2}.$ We have that ${n}_{2}=j,$ and therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}(-x\\,i+2y\\,j)\\cdot j\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}y\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a line integral with respect to arc length, which we can evaluate in the usual way. Parameterizing the side ${C}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\nr(t)=t\\,i+2\\,j,\\,⇒\\,{r}^{′}(t)=i,\\,t\\in [-2,2].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}y\\,\\text{d}s & =2{\\int }_{-2}^{2}2\\cdot ||{r}^{′}(t)||\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy symmetry, the flux integral across the side ${C}_{4}$ must be the same. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{4}}F\\cdot {n}_{4}\\,\\text{d}s=16.\n$$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s=2\\cdot (-8)+2\\cdot 16=16.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-600bf7ec-a1e3-56fd-89d4-4751fb47440c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-600bf7ec-a1e3-56fd-89d4-4751fb47440c" :answer-field/id #uuid "600bf7ec-a1e3-56fd-89d4-4751fb47440c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e135fd94-1acc-52d5-ad78-5d64f964e29a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-03305bbd-2ed9-5a18-8c72-9c0d0c631c78" "answer-e135fd94-1acc-52d5-ad78-5d64f964e29a" "answer-78c29a36-9fe5-5900-be19-eb34c038c994" "answer-e888d5f3-7dc6-5267-ad8c-2c21bc41dcbd" "answer-97e1e9e0-3fe5-5a2d-b26c-2e7b570ac0c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03305bbd-2ed9-5a18-8c72-9c0d0c631c78" :answer/id #uuid "03305bbd-2ed9-5a18-8c72-9c0d0c631c78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e135fd94-1acc-52d5-ad78-5d64f964e29a" :answer/id #uuid "e135fd94-1acc-52d5-ad78-5d64f964e29a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78c29a36-9fe5-5900-be19-eb34c038c994" :answer/id #uuid "78c29a36-9fe5-5900-be19-eb34c038c994" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e888d5f3-7dc6-5267-ad8c-2c21bc41dcbd" :answer/id #uuid "e888d5f3-7dc6-5267-ad8c-2c21bc41dcbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97e1e9e0-3fe5-5a2d-b26c-2e7b570ac0c3" :answer/id #uuid "97e1e9e0-3fe5-5a2d-b26c-2e7b570ac0c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}]
